  "body": "CENTRAL-24/25 representation follow-up: the shared named-stock scopes are scientifically supported, but `PARTIAL` is not the native value for an unstated complete ingredient list. Use `UNKNOWN` where the source merely names a preparation. Preserve the original author packet unchanged; its `decisions.json` common-publication condition recommending blanket `PARTIAL` is superseded by this qualification.\n\nThe same concrete field remains in frozen controls941 (`tris_hcl_0_2m_ph7_5_dsmz273`) and955 (`hepes_2m_ph7_jcm556_1200`): the cited recipes name those stocks and do not explicitly say additional constituents are omitted. Their boundary conclusions remain valid; their completeness metadata requires a scoped correction before application. Controls280/938 have more detailed preparation evidence and need individual reading, not a blanket enum replacement. Full named-input Wolfe/Hutner lists must not be downgraded solely because hydration, amount, or final species are uncertain. Preserve all source/physical/role/export holds; this adds no chemistry or gate rule.\n\nExact independent evidence: `preflight/central24-25-independent-v1/findings.json` and native review. No worker or maintained file was edited.\n\nIndependent review supports all ten bounded nominal conventions and preserves twelve comparison scopes. The source guidance and controls correction is recorded before the accountable source-worker fix. Native review binds56targets/587inputs; all56 original records pass closed schema. Evidence: `preflight/central24-25-independent-v1/HANDOFF.json` SHA256 `7a24f3cf7a8229028ec7091be34a99e78e0e13b67832a383e1cfc6767ce275dc`; manifest `90ad498a098dbe1d4b1a446be09242ceba6649b53b2136e0d6cb65ad6c30d363`, all50 members rehashed by coordinator. Ten guarded drafts are separately under final-candidate review; no maintained application or release has occurred.\n",
